# Sync docs with every change

When you change product behavior (CLI flags, hub UI, GitHub auth, agents, clone-and-go, triage), update the same-PR docs in the same turn. Do not leave README/docs describing the old path.

Always check:

- `README.md` — clone steps, requirements, hub, commands, troubleshooting
- `docs/providers.md` — how agents and GitHub access work
- `docs/pipeline.md` — if the review flow changed
- `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` — agent-facing how-to
- `.cursor/skills/review-pr/SKILL.md` — if the chat/hub workflow changed
- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — only if contributor commands changed

Match the product: `pnpm prsm` starts the hub; public PRs need no `gh`; private repos use hub **Connect GitHub**; agents are added from the hub. Do not document a required `gh auth login` or `pnpm build` before first hub start unless that is actually true again.
